# Chromium's language follows macOS's, as in Chrome and Arc (#167): its own pages and dialogs, and the language
# extensions show (chrome.i18n picks their _locales by it). On the Chrome engine Chromium took the language from
# Cra's app bundle, which carries no translations, so it stayed English whatever macOS was set to (GitHub #484).
# Here macOS's language is Chinese (Simplified) for Cra alone.
# promise: #484
budget rss=600
arg -AppleLanguages
arg (zh-Hans-CN)
extension ${FIXTURES}/Extension
expect-log chromium locale: zh-CN for zh-Hans-CN
cra://open?url=chrome://extensions
wait 3
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"'chrome pages in '.concat(document.documentElement.lang)"}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*chrome pages in [a-zA-Z-]+
reject-log chrome pages in en
cra://open?url=chrome-extension://${EXTENSION_ID}/options.html
wait 2
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"'extensions in '.concat(chrome.i18n.getUILanguage())"}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*extensions in zh-CN
